        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Position-Specific Iterated (PSI)-BLAST is the most sensitive BLAST program, making it useful for finding very distantly related proteins or new members of a protein family. Use PSI-BLAST when your standard protein-protein BLAST search either failed to find significant hits, or returned hits with descriptions such as &quot;hypothetical protein&quot; or &quot;similar to...&quot;.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>NIH BLAST homepage</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PSI-BLAST</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


