            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">The functions in this R extension are intended for cross-study comparison of gene expression array data. Required from the user is gene expression matrices, their corresponding gene-id vectors and other useful information, and they could be &apos;list&apos;,&apos;matrix&apos;, or &apos;ExpressionSet&apos;. The main function is &apos;mergeExprs&apos; which transforms the input objects into data in the merged format, such that common genes in different datasets can be easily found. And the function &apos;intcor&apos; calculate the correlation coefficients. Other functions use the output from &apos;modelOutcome&apos; to graphically display the results and cross-validate associations of gene expression data with survival.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.4/bioc/html/MergeMaid.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <terms:creator>Nandini Badarinarayan</terms:creator>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MergeMaid</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


